cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Spectral Krylov-JEPA: Krylov-Subspace Joint-Embedding Pretraining for Few-Shot Quantum Eigenstate Prediction"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-26"
license: MIT
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Contributors
    given-names: Spectral Krylov-JEPA
abstract: >-
  Research software evaluating whether self-supervised pretraining on
  inexpensive Lanczos/Krylov trajectories improves few-shot prediction of
  low-energy eigenstates of 2D Schrödinger operators relative to matched
  baselines (scratch, Field-JEPA, Operator-JEPA).
keywords:
  - JEPA
  - Krylov subspace
  - Lanczos
  - Schrödinger equation
  - self-supervised learning
  - few-shot learning
